      "sourceTextSha256": "cd82198f9837ba78bc70f1b3391dcec2cc29b40655c8d1f0f9d8cfbc2084698a",
      "text": "Breakfast at the hotel. At 09:00, set out on a sightseeing tour of Lima that includes a visit to Casa Aliaga.\n\nBegin in Miraflores with a visit to the Park of Love, a view of the Huaca Pucllana archaeological complex from an observation point and a walk through the Olive Grove Park. Colonial mansions still line the neighbourhood’s streets.\n\nIn the historic centre, the route takes you through Plaza Mayor, where you will see the Cathedral, the Presidential Palace and City Hall. The itinerary also includes the Monastery and Church of San Francisco.\n\nStep inside Casa Aliaga, a historic private residence built in 1536 for Jerónimo de Aliaga, an associate of Francisco Pizarro, on the site of a pre-Columbian structure. The house has belonged to the same family for nearly five centuries. Its interiors, antique furniture and artworks offer a glimpse into the lives of the Spanish aristocracy in colonial Peru.\n\nAfter the tour, transfer to the airport for your flight to Cusco, the former Inca capital. On arrival, you will be met and taken to the 4-star Xima Cusco or a similar hotel.",
